From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: valentin rameau <valentin.rameau@outlook.fr>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:53:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 14/33] Treat page 0/1 execution as off the rails

The bank test alone cannot see a jump into the stack: banks $00-$3F mirror
WRAM below $2000, so landing at $03:01F1 is a mapped address and looks
legitimate. Titles that keep no code in page 0 or 1 -- direct page and stack
only -- are better served by treating that as a crossing, so the approach
capture names the transfer that produced it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c b/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
index 841f61a..1a389fd 100644
--- a/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
+++ b/runner/src/snes/interp_bridge.c
@@ -1841,6 +1841,13 @@ static int _interp_run_core(CpuState *cpu, uint32_t entry_pc24,
               uint8_t _bank = (uint8_t)(pc_before >> 16);
               int _mapped = (_bank <= 0x07) || (_bank >= 0x80 && _bank <= 0x87) ||
                             _bank == 0x7E || _bank == 0x7F;
+              /* Executing in page 0 or 1 is off the rails too, and the bank
+               * test alone never sees it: banks $00-$3F mirror WRAM below
+               * $2000, so a jump into the stack page lands at a *mapped*
+               * address like $03:01F1 and looks legitimate. This title keeps
+               * no code there -- direct page and stack only -- so treat it as
+               * a crossing and capture the approach that produced it. */
+              if ((pc_before & 0xFFFFu) < 0x0200u) _mapped = 0;
               if (s_prev_mapped && !_mapped)
                 interp_bridge_note_offrails_vita(s_prev_pc, s_prev_op, s_prev_sp,
                                                  pc_before, op);
